# CI verification (Cursor)

Before finishing any code change, run the **standard CI gate** from repo root.
Canonical list: `orchestra/ci_gate.py` (`CI_CHECKS`). Mirrors `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
jobs `code-formatting` + `ut-venv` — **not** nightly workflows.

```bash
uv run ruff format --check .
uv run ruff check .
uv run mypy .
uv run pytest tests/ -v
```

## Not sufficient

- `pytest -m "not slow"` — local shortcut only; CI runs the full suite
- `mypy quant_rl/` or `ruff check quant_rl/` — CI checks the whole tree (`.`)

## Test mocks

Use `monkeypatch.setattr(obj, "method", fn)`. Do **not** assign to bound methods
(`obj.method = fn`); `mypy .` fails with `method-assign`.

## Orchestra / CI runners

GitHub runners may lack agent CLIs (`opencode`, `vibe`, etc.). Orchestra tests must
stub binaries via `stub_clis` in `tests/test_orchestra/conftest.py`.
